WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.840
Type 2 diabetes is a condition
in which your blood sugar

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.940
level is too high.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.740
After you eat foods that
contain carbohydrates,

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.010
chemicals in your
small intestine

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:27.350
break them down into single
sugar molecules called glucose.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.890
Next, the cells lining
your small intestine

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:37.900
absorb the glucose, which
passes into the bloodstream.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.469
When the blood
reaches your pancreas,

00:00:40.469 --> 00:00:45.150
beta cells inside the pancreas
detect the rising glucose

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.350
levels.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.320
To reduce the glucose
level, your beta cells

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.500
release insulin into
your bloodstream.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.180
As the blood circulates
through your body,

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:00.510
the insulin and glucose
exit the bloodstream

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:05.200
into your tissues to
reach your body's cells.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.330
Most cells of the body
have certain receptors

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:13.390
on their surface that bind
to the circulating insulin.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:16.540
Insulin acts like
a key in a lock

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.060
to open up the cell so that
the circulating glucose can

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.590
get inside the cell.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.200
Now, your cell can
use the glucose

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:31.500
to produce the energy it
needs to function properly.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:36.040
If you have type 2 diabetes,
either your pancreas

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.010
does not produce enough
insulin or your body's cells

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:44.200
resist its effects or both.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:49.770
If you have insulin resistance,
your insulin cannot unlock

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:53.520
the cells to let glucose
in because the locks,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.770
called receptors, are
abnormal or missing.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:02.890
As a result, glucose is
locked out of your cells.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.340
Consequently, the
amount of glucose

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:08.640
builds up in your bloodstream
in a condition called

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.460
hyperglycemia.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.040
To compensate for
hyperglycemia, your pancreas

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.690
produces more and more insulin.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:22.660
Your overworked beta cells try
to keep up with the demand,

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:28.710
but gradually lose their ability
to produce enough insulin.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:32.020
Due to hyperglycemia
and the lack of insulin,

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.080
you may experience the
following classic symptoms

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:40.050
of diabetes-- excessive
hunger, excessive thirst,

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:45.810
increased urine volume, and
unexplained weight loss.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.810
Symptoms of type 2 diabetes
that may appear over time

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:56.020
include fatigue, recurrent
infections, changes in vision,

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:58.820
itching, and
tingling or prickling

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.500
sensations in your skin.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:06.590
Life threatening complications
of type 2 diabetes

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:11.600
include diabetic
ketoacidosis, hyperosmolar

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:18.900
hyperglycemic nonketotic
syndrome, and hypoglycemia.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.910
If you don't receive
treatment for hyperglycemia,

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:26.400
diabetic ketoacidosis
can result.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.570
Because you no longer have
enough insulin circulating

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.780
in your blood, your
cells can't get

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:35.000
the glucose they need
to produce energy.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.780
As a result, your body
turns to fats and proteins

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.780
as an alternative
source of energy.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.080
During the fat
breakdown process,

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.250
certain byproducts,
known as ketone bodies,

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.730
accumulate in your
blood, resulting

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:52.900
in a condition called ketosis.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.010
If ketones build up to
dangerously high levels

00:03:56.010 --> 00:04:00.600
in your bloodstream, you may
develop diabetic ketoacidosis,

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:06.160
or DKA, which can lead
to coma and death.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.830
Another complication
resulting from failure

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:12.550
to treat hyperglycemia
is called hyperosmolar

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:17.670
hyperglycemic nonketotic
syndrome, or HHNS.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:20.370
As the insulin
deficiency continues,

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:23.870
your blood glucose
level increases.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:28.340
In response, your kidneys filter
excess glucose out of the blood

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:32.870
into urine, along with
large amounts of water.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.500
Unless you consume
large amounts of water,

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.630
your kidneys cannot keep up
with the demand of removing

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.470
the glucose from your
bloodstream and diluting it

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:44.770
sufficiently in urine.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:48.360
As a result, your blood
becomes much more concentrated

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:52.370
than normal, a condition
called hyperosmolarity.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:55.410
Hyperosmolarity pulls
water out of your body

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:59.970
tissues into your bloodstream,
causing severe dehydration,

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.800
which may lead to hyperosmolar
hyperglycemic nonketotic

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:04.980
syndrome.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:11.200
Neurological symptoms, such as
seizures and coma, can occur.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:15.730
If you take an excessive
dose of diabetic medication,

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:18.390
you may experience
an acute complication

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:22.370
called hypoglycemia
or insulin shock.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:26.330
Excessive insulin or oral
hypoglycemic medication

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.630
causes too much glucose
to go into cells,

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:35.100
leaving an insufficient
amount in your bloodstream.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.900
Certain organs,
such as the brain,

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.900
need a constant energy
supply to function properly.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.950
Because the brain's primary
source of energy is glucose,

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:51.170
it is the first organ affected
by lower glucose levels.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.810
When your brain
cells, called neurons,

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:58.310
are starved for glucose,
they start to malfunction,

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:02.000
causing symptoms such as
nervousness, shakiness,

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.630
and confusion.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:07.640
If your glucose level
continues to drop,

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.060
the electrical activity
of your neurons

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.700
diminishes
significantly, resulting

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:17.080
in seizures or diabetic coma.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.950
Over time, chronic
poorly controlled

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:24.130
type 2 diabetes can cause
degenerative tissue damage,

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:27.140
resulting in long
term complications

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:32.220
such as atherosclerosis,
blindness, neuropathy,

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:35.340
and renal failure.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:38.800
To avoid the complications
of type 2 diabetes,

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.490
you can take steps to
keep your glucose level

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:45.590
within a normal range using a
combination of blood glucose

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:51.190
monitoring, a healthy
diet, regular exercise,

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:55.370
and medications as necessary.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:58.430
You will need to check the
level of glucose in your blood

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.870
frequently with a glucometer.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.850
To do this, you will
prick your finger

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:05.150
with a small needle
called a lancet

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.080
and place a drop of blood
on the strip attached

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.700
to the glucometer.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.820
Based on your blood
glucose level,

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:15.370
you may need to adjust your
meals, physical activity,

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.290
or medication dose.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:21.800
Eating a healthy diet will help
to lower your glucose level

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:25.870
when you eat a diet rich in
fruits, vegetables, and whole

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:30.660
grains, have meals and snacks
about the same time every day,

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:34.200
consume the right balance
of carbohydrates, proteins,

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:40.200
and fat, and minimize your
intake of high sugar foods.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:44.100
Getting regular exercise--
even just 30 minutes

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:47.090
a day-- will lower your
blood glucose level,

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:53.220
decrease insulin resistance,
and may lead to weight loss.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:56.710
You may need to take one or
more diabetic medications

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:59.530
to help lower blood glucose.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:02.830
Some of these medications
increase insulin production

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:05.600
in your pancreas.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:08.040
Others decrease
insulin resistance

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:10.570
in your skeletal muscles.

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:16.050
Some treatments increase insulin
sensitivity in certain tissues.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:19.040
Others promote a slight
decrease in absorption

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:23.370
of glucose in your
digestive system.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:27.290
If your type 2 diabetes cannot
be controlled with diet,

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:31.090
exercise, and oral medications,
your doctor may prescribe

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:37.580
insulin and train you to
inject it just under your skin.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.899
By treating and controlling
your blood glucose level,

00:08:40.899 --> 00:08:43.680
you may prevent the
occurrence of complications

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:46.010
from type 2 diabetes.

